//VSAMCHK  JOB (POC),'VSAM SPACE CHECK',CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X
//*
//* ------------------------------------------------------------------
//*  WHICH VOLUMES DOES THE VSAM CATALOG ALREADY OWN?
//*
//*  DEFINE CLUSTER FAILED WITH  IDC3033I VOLUME RECORD NOT FOUND IN
//*  CATALOG.  ON MVS 3.8 VSAM USES VSAM CATALOGS, AND A CATALOG MUST
//*  OWN A VOLUME - RECORDED AS A VOLUME RECORD, CREATED BY DEFINE
//*  SPACE - BEFORE A CLUSTER CAN BE SUBALLOCATED THERE.
//*
//*  LISTCAT SPACE LISTS THE SPACE (VOLUME) ENTRIES: THE VOLUMES THE
//*  CATALOG OWNS AND THE DATA SPACES ON THEM.
//*
//*  WHAT TO LOOK FOR:
//*    - ANY VOLUME LISTED AT ALL.  IF ONE HAS FREE SPACE, POINT
//*      jcl/DEFCTL.jcl AT IT AND NOTHING ELSE IS NEEDED.
//*    - IF NOTHING IS LISTED, NO VOLUME IS OWNED YET AND
//*      jcl/DEFSPACE.jcl HAS TO RUN FIRST.
//*
//*  ALSO WORTH RUNNING AT THE MVS CONSOLE:   D U,DASD,ONLINE
//*  WHICH SHOWS WHICH VOLUMES ACTUALLY EXIST.
//* ------------------------------------------------------------------
//LISTC   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD  *
  LISTCAT SPACE ALL
/*
